; Dungeons of Daggorath -- P17 M1: the dungeon and the view, M2: the
; command line and the clock, M3: objects, and M4: creatures.
;
;   load "daggorath
;   daggorath
;
; docs/daggorath-design.md is the design; this file is M1 to M4's
; slice of it -- section 15: M1 is "the cell walk, the architectural lists,
; MOVE and TURN with both animations, the grey ramp, the inverted levels
; including the status bar, and hw.setcpu "fast with restore.clock behind
; it"; M2 is "the scheduler of section 5, the parser (PARSER.ASM/
; TOKEN.ASM), the text furniture of sections 4.1b-4.1c, the heart drawn and
; beating, fainting, damage recovery, death"; M3 is "OCBs, the bag, two
; hands, GET PULL STOW DROP EXAMINE USE REVEAL INCANT, the status line,
; weight, torches and both light channels, the map and both scrolls"; M4
; is "the CCB table, CMOVE and its preference walk, the peek-a-boo, combat
; both ways, creature loot, death, and the approach sounds of section 9.3."
;
; YOU START IN THE DARK, and that is M3's doing rather than a fault: the
; player's own light is zero (COMDAT.ASM never sets PRLITE), so until you
; PULL the pine torch out of the bag and USE it, RLIGHT is 0 and
; VCTLST.ASM:SETFAX draws nothing at any range. The ROM's own attract mode
; opens EXAMINE / PULL RIGHT TORCH / USE RIGHT / LOOK (TOKEN.ASM:AUTTAB)
; for exactly this reason.
;
; M4 is what makes the dungeon worth walking into: NEWLVL.ASM:NLVL40 now
; runs, so the loot every object was born holding (ONCE.ASM:CINI40 marks
; all sixty-three creature-owned) is on the monsters, and killing one is
; the only way to get any of it.
;
; This file does NOT include (each is a later milestone by design section
; 15):
;   - ladders/holes/VFTTAB (M5) -- the forward view always draws the plain
;     ceiling line (VERT.ASM:CELINE), and the map marks no vertical
;     features. INCANT transforms the Ring of Ohm but does not end the
;     game: PINCAN.ASM:WINNER is M5's, with the wizards.
;   - sound (M6) -- every SITE is here and goes through `dagg.sound`,
;     which records SOUNDS.ASM's own SNDTAB index and volume; what is
;     missing is the generator behind the index (design section 9.2) and
;     the heartbeat thump on voices 0 and 4 (section 9.4).
;   - three of the fifteen commands, which is why `dagg.soon` exists:
;     CLIMB, ZLOAD and ZSAVE, all M5.
;
; `make "dagg.pace 1` before `daggorath` runs the creatures at the ROM's
; raw table; 2 is the default and is what a board settled on beside the
; memory of the original -- see dagg.creature.delay. It touches creature
; turns only, never the heart, the torch or your own commands.
;
; The maze, the object and creature tables and every vector list are
; generated into this file
; by scripts/gen_daggorath.py -- see the marked block below. There is no
; second file to ship and nothing to open at run time.

;==========================================================================
; The scale tables -- design section 6.1, verbatim (also tests/logo/p17m0,
; where the transform this file reuses was board-confirmed at M0).

make "dagg.norscl [200 128 80 50 31 20 12 8 4 2]
make "dagg.hlfscl [255 156 100 65 40 26 16 10 6 3]

; BAKSCL, VIEWER.ASM: "the same table shifted one entry along" -- the
; second through eleventh entries of the eleven-value HLFSCL/BAKSCL block
; VIEWER.ASM lays out (the eleventh, marked *DEBUG in the source, is
; BAKSCL's own last entry, not dead data once the table is read this way).
make "dagg.bakscl [156 100 65 40 26 16 10 6 3 1]

; VECTOR.ASM's fade table (design section 8), the dash column -- P18 M2's
; `setpendash` makes a dotted stroke cost the same as a solid one, so dots
; are M1's default (the grey alternative is M1a, optional, not built here).
;
; It is BITMSK read through two of VECTOR.ASM's own quirks. SETFAX loads
; `BITMSK+8` indexed by A, and A only ever reaches -6 there (the `CMPA #-7
; / BLE` above it takes the darkness branch first), so the six entries used
; are BIT0 through BIT5 -- 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32. VECTOR then does `INC
; VCTFAD` before loading FADCNT from it, so the PERIOD is one more than the
; table byte: 2, 3, 5, 9, 17, 33. There is no 65 -- design section 8 lists
; one, reading BITMSK as though A reached -7, and that entry is unreachable
; because -7 is already total darkness.
make "dagg.dash [1 2 3 5 9 17 33]

; The two light channels -- CD.ASM's RLIGHT/MLIGHT and PRLITE/PMLITE,
; design section 8.3. PRLITE is the player's OWN light and COMDAT.ASM never
; sets it, so it is zero: with no burning torch the whole dungeon is dark.
; PUPDAT.ASM:PSUB10 adds the torch's two XXXTAB values on top of it, and
; that sum is what SETFAX attenuates by range.
;
; MAGFLG is the channel selector, set for one vector list at a time by
; whatever is about to draw something magical -- a secret door
; (VIEWER.ASM:VIEW22), a floor object (VIEW52, which draws it twice, once
; under each channel), or a magical creature (CMRDRW, M4). SETFAX consumes
; and clears it, which is why it is set immediately before a draw and never
; anywhere else.
make "dagg.prlite 0
make "dagg.prmlite 0
make "dagg.light 0
make "dagg.mlight 0
make "dagg.magflg "false

;==========================================================================
; The maze and the architectural vector lists.
